---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro'
import Layout from '../../components/Layout.astro'
import BlogPostShell from '../../components/BlogPostShell.astro'
import BlogToolEmbed from '../../components/BlogToolEmbed.astro'

const slug = 'luminous-energy-converter'
const seo = {
  title: 'Luminous energy converter — lm·s, talbots | maratool',
  description: 'Convert lumen-seconds, talbots, lumen-minutes, and lumen-hours instantly. Free browser luminous energy converter.',
  canonical: `https://maratool.com/blog/${slug}`,
  schema: {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BlogPosting',
    headline: 'How to convert lumen-seconds, talbots, and lumen-hours',
    image: 'https://maratool.com/og/converter.svg',
    datePublished: '2026-07-25',
    dateModified: '2026-07-25',
    author: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'Marcell Almeida', url: 'https://marcell.com.br' },
    publisher: {
      '@type': 'Organization',
      name: 'maratool',
      url: 'https://maratool.com',
      logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: 'https://maratool.com/favicon.svg' },
    },
    mainEntityOfPage: { '@type': 'WebPage', '@id': `https://maratool.com/blog/${slug}` },
    url: `https://maratool.com/blog/${slug}`,
    description: 'Convert lumen-seconds, talbots, lumen-minutes, and lumen-hours instantly. Free browser luminous energy converter.',
  },
  breadcrumbSchema: {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://maratool.com' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Blog', item: 'https://maratool.com/blog' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'How to convert lumen-seconds, talbots, and lumen-hours', item: `https://maratool.com/blog/${slug}` },
    ],
  },
}
---
<Base {...seo}>
  <Layout>
    <BlogPostShell
      title="How to convert lumen-seconds, talbots, and lumen-hours"
      lead="Type a luminous energy — read lm·s, talbots, lm·min, or lm·h instantly."
      date="July 25, 2026"
      dateIso="2026-07-25"
    >
      <p>Luminous energy is light flux integrated over time — what a camera flash or UV-cure lamp actually delivers. The <a href="/luminous-energy-converter">Luminous Energy Converter</a> handles the second/minute/hour steps exactly.</p>

      <BlogToolEmbed slug="luminous-energy-converter" title="Try it — convert luminous energy units" height={440} />

      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Pick units</strong> — "Lumen-hour (lm·h)" to "Lumen-second (lm·s)", or any other pair.</li>
        <li><strong>Type a value</strong> — the result updates as you type, with swap and copy.</li>
        <li><strong>Copy</strong> — one click, with "Copied!" feedback.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Luminous energy conversion factors</h2>
      <p>Every unit converts through the lumen-second (the base unit). To convert A → B, multiply by A's factor and divide by B's:</p>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Unit</th><th>= this many lumen-seconds</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        <tr><td>Kilolumen-second (klm·s)</td><td>1,000</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Lumen-second (lm·s)</td><td>1</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Talbot (T)</td><td>1</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Lumen-minute (lm·min)</td><td>60</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Lumen-hour (lm·h)</td><td>3,600</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>When you need it</h2>
      <p>A 1,000 lm bulb running one hour emits 1,000 lm·h = 3.6 million lm·s. A speedlight dumping 60 lm·s does in a millisecond what that bulb does in 60 ms — which is why flashes freeze motion.</p>

      <h2>Sources & methodology</h2>
      <p>Conversion factors follow <a href="https://www.bipm.org/en/publications/si-brochure" rel="noopener" target="_blank">BIPM SI Brochure</a>; exact-by-definition factors are marked in the tool itself. All math runs client-side in your browser — nothing is uploaded.</p>

      <h2>More conversion guides</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/blog/luminous-flux-converter">How to convert lumens, kilolumens, and cd·sr</a></li>
        <li><a href="/blog/illuminance-converter">How to convert lux to foot-candles</a></li>
        <li><a href="/blog/energy-converter">How to convert calories, joules, kWh, and BTU</a></li>
      </ul>
      <p>Or browse everything at once in the <a href="/blog/new-unit-converters">new unit &amp; sizing converters roundup</a>.</p>

      <hr class="blog-divider" />
      <p class="blog-footer-note">The <a href="/luminous-energy-converter">Luminous Energy</a> tool is free, runs locally, and never sends your data to a server. More <a href="/converter">converter tools</a> at <a href="/">maratool.com</a>.</p>
    </BlogPostShell>
  </Layout>
</Base>
